<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donato Bramante</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1444">1444</a>–<a href="/years/1514">1514</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Bramante</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donato Bramante was an Italian architect and painter, born near Urbino, who worked at the Sforza court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from the late 1470s until 1499, building the church of Santa Maria presso San Satiro and the domed tribune of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-maria-delle-grazie-milan">Santa Maria delle Grazie</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> he became the leading architect of the High <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>, designing the Tempietto and the first plan of the new St Peter's Basilica for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donato-bramante.jpg" alt="Donato Bramante" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donato_Bramante.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
